# Service registry — the global catalogue of every stack the agent can render.
#
# entrypoint.sh reads this to turn the per-host AGENT_SERVICES list (a space- or
# comma-separated set of service names) into a generated agent config at startup.
# Adding a stack = ONE row here; a host opts in by adding the name to its
# AGENT_SERVICES. No per-host config files.
#
# Pipe-delimited, one row per service. Lines starting with # and blank lines are
# ignored. Columns:
#
#   service | project | env | folder | dest | type
#
#   service  name used in AGENT_SERVICES (and the custom .tpl basename for type=custom)
#   project  Infisical project id (UUID)
#   env      Infisical environment slug (always prod here)
#   folder   Infisical secret path; may contain ${AGENT_HOST} (substituted at runtime)
#   dest     output file under /dev/shm/ — MUST match what the consumer stack's
#            compose reads via env_file (don't rename without updating the consumer)
#   type     dump   = render the WHOLE folder as KEY=VALUE via listSecrets (default)
#            custom = use the hand-written files/configs/templates/<service>.tpl as-is
#                     (for renamed/duplicated keys, host-scoped paths, or raw-value files)
#
# Folder dump only reproduces a stack's env correctly when the Infisical secret
# names already equal the consumer's env-var names. Where they differ — or the
# output isn't KEY=VALUE — the row is type=custom and keeps its own template.

# service                | project                              | env  | folder                           | dest                              | type

# --- Apps project (2f0eb3d1) ---
postgres                 | 2f0eb3d1-3e2a-4ce7-8060-5e47ad877e47 | prod | /postgres                        | postgres.env                      | dump
paperless                | 2f0eb3d1-3e2a-4ce7-8060-5e47ad877e47 | prod | /paperless                       | apps_paperless.env                | dump
